# rtmux per-machine configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` next to rtmux.zsh (the copy is gitignored) and adjust. All
# values may also be set as plain environment variables, which take precedence
# over this file. Everything is optional — `rtmux <host>` works with no .env
# at all.
#
#   RTMUX_HOST  — the *default single remote* used by a bare `rtmux`.
#   RTMUX_HOSTS — the fan-out *pool* (space-separated ssh aliases or
#                 user@host). Used by a bare `rtmux` only when RTMUX_HOST is
#                 unset, or any time with `rtmux --all`.
#
# With both set: bare `rtmux` gives you the fast single-host picker on
# RTMUX_HOST, and `rtmux --all` merges the whole pool into the tabbed picker.
# Leave RTMUX_HOST unset to make a bare `rtmux` always fan out over the pool.
typeset RTMUX_HOST="dev"                      # default single remote (alias or user@host)
typeset RTMUX_HOSTS="dev prod"                # fan-out pool for --all / no-default

# Optional knobs (shown with their defaults):
# typeset RTMUX_WATCH=1                       # 1 = live-refresh the picker, 0 = off
# typeset RTMUX_WATCH_INTERVAL=1              # seconds between refreshes (fractional ok)
# typeset RTMUX_CODE_DIR="~/code"             # remote project root for the -n name match
